    {
      "_type": "UMLActivity",
      "_id": "61c321be2a864cfdb46f49f5ec816e58",
      "_parent": {
        "$ref": "b48d511fdf5c4362b38d22885a73461f"
      },
      "name": "AD-05 - Update Medicine Price",
      "visibility": "public",
      "isAbstract": false,
      "isReadOnly": false,
      "isSingleExecution": false,
      "documentation": "Activity Diagram derived from UC-13 (Update Medicine Price).\nShows the workflow through which an authorised Pharmacist / Pharmacy Staff member updates the reported/indicative price information for a medicine associated with their pharmacy.\n\nPreconditions:\n1. The user is authenticated.\n2. The user has the required pharmacy-side authority.\n3. The relevant pharmacy context is available.\n4. The medicine can be identified within the MedAccess catalogue/workflow.\n\nPostconditions (success): The medicine's reported price information for the relevant pharmacy is updated; the accepted price becomes the current price information used by relevant MedAccess workflows; relevant update metadata/time is recorded where supported; the user receives confirmation.\nPostconditions (failure): The previous valid price information is not incorrectly overwritten; the user is informed the update was not completed; the user can correct invalid input where appropriate.\n\nScope boundary: MedAccess maintains reported medicine price information for the relevant pharmacy; it does not perform a sale, payment transaction, or purchasing operation. Stock changes belong to AD-04 - Update Medicine Stock. Patient/Caregiver price viewing and comparison belongs to AD-02.\n\nTraceability: AD-05 -> UC-13 - Update Medicine Price.",
      "ownedElements": [
